Cudy TR3600 v1: fix the PWM fan channel (1 -> 0)

The board DTS wired the pwm-fan to PWM channel 1 and used the pwm1_pins
pinctrl group. On real hardware the fan is driven by PWM0 (PIN13), which
is the pwm_pins group already defined in mt7987.dtsi.

Symptom with the wrong channel: the kernel pwm-fan driver binds but the
hwmon cooling device never appears (no PWM output at all), and the
thermal governor cannot control the fan. LuCI reports
"The PWM fan cooling device was not detected." and the fan either stays
off or, depending on the boot state, spins uncontrolled.

Verified on device: after this change /sys/kernel/debug/pwm shows
"pwm-0 (pwm-fan): requested enabled period: 50000 ns duty: ..." and the
pwm-fan cooling device is registered (max_state=3).

Signed-off-by: TR3600 build kit <noreply@example.com>
---
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@
 
 &fan {
 	fan-supply = <&fan_3p3v>;
-	pwms = <&pwm 1 50000 0>;
+	pwms = <&pwm 0 50000 0>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@
 
 &pwm {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&pwm1_pins>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pwm_pins>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
